# Error Standards

## Error Categories

Every error in an n8n workflow belongs to one of these categories:

| Category | Code | Description | Default Action |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Config** | `ERR_CONFIG` | Wrong node setup, type mismatch, missing required field | Fix configuration, do not retry |
| **Data** | `ERR_DATA` | Unexpected input shape, missing required field, invalid value | Validate upstream, send to DLQ |
| **Auth** | `ERR_AUTH` | Invalid credential, expired token, insufficient permissions | Alert ops, do not retry automatically |
| **Integration** | `ERR_INTEGRATION` | External service timeout, 5xx, network error | Retry with backoff, alert after N failures |
| **Logic** | `ERR_LOGIC` | Unexpected branch reached, assertion failed, infinite loop | Alert dev, stop execution |
| **Resource** | `ERR_RESOURCE` | Rate limit (429), quota exceeded, storage full | Exponential backoff, alert |

## Standard Error Object

All error notifications must include this structure:

```json
{
  "error": {
    "category": "ERR_INTEGRATION",
    "workflow": "{{ $workflow.name }}",
    "node": "{{ $node.name }}",
    "executionId": "{{ $execution.id }}",
    "message": "{{ $json.error.message }}",
    "timestamp": "{{ $now.toISO() }}",
    "input": "{{ $json }}"
  }
}
```

## Retry Policy by Category

| Category | Retry? | Max Retries | Backoff |
|---|---|---|---|
| Config | No | 0 | — |
| Data | No | 0 | — |
| Auth | No | 0 | — |
| Integration | Yes | 3 | Exponential (1s, 2s, 4s) |
| Logic | No | 0 | — |
| Resource | Yes | 5 | Exponential (5s, 10s, 20s...) |

## Error Handling Architecture

### Every workflow MUST have:

```
[Error Trigger]
      ↓
[Format Error Message]   ← uses Standard Error Object above
      ↓
[Notify Ops]             ← Slack, email, or webhook
```

### Recommended: Dead Letter Queue pattern for data errors

```
[Validate Input]
      ↓ (invalid)
[Send to DLQ]            ← store in DB or Notion for manual review
      ↓
[Notify for Review]
```

## Node-Level Error Handling

### HTTP Request nodes

```
[HTTP Request]
      ↓ (on error: continue)
[Check Status]           ← IF node: statusCode >= 400
      ↓ (true)
[Handle HTTP Error]      ← categorize as ERR_INTEGRATION or ERR_AUTH
```

### AI Agent nodes

```
[AI Agent]
      ↓
[Validate Output]        ← Code node or IF: check response format
      ↓ (invalid)
[Handle Agent Error]     ← categorize as ERR_DATA
```

## Error Message Standards

Error notifications must be:
- **Actionable**: include what failed and what to do about it
- **Traceable**: include execution ID for debugging
- **Contextual**: include the input that caused the error (redact PII)

Template for Slack/email notifications:

```
🔴 Workflow Error: {workflow name}
Node: {node name}
Type: {error category}
Message: {error message}
Execution: {execution ID}
Time: {timestamp}

Next step: {link to debug runbook or n8n execution URL}
```
